          "type": "conceptbox",
          "variant": "",
          "html": "<ul>\n<li>Population = everything; sample = what you measured. Parameter describes the population, statistic describes the sample</li>\n<li>Stratified sampling protects against class imbalance; cross-validation (k-fold) checks generalisation and detects overfitting</li>\n<li>Sample variance divides by <strong>n − 1</strong>, not n</li>\n<li>Quartile method in the lecture notes ≠ the method software packages use — use the lecture method for hand calculations</li>\n<li>Fences: UIF = Q3 + 1.5×IQR, LIF = Q1 − 1.5×IQR; whiskers stop at the nearest real data point inside the fence, not at the fence itself</li>\n<li>Mean &gt; median → right skew; mean &lt; median → left skew</li>\n<li>Not every outlier should be removed — investigate first</li>\n<li>Normalisation → fixed range (e.g. 0–1); standardisation → mean 0, standard deviation 1</li>\n</ul>",
